        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0177" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg53"/>

                <head>No. 35.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Delaplaine to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 1, 1881</date>.
                        (Received April 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 453.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to dispatch No. 438, I herewith
                    inclose a copy of the reply (received to-day) of the imperial and royal minister
                    for foreign affairs to Mr. Kasson’s note of March 18, 1881, the latter
                    containing a formal protest against the official order of prohibition of the
                    importation of swine meat and swine products from the United States into
                    Austria-Hungary.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. F. DELAPLAINE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d35-a1.xml" xpointer="d35-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
